{"uid":"cli/commands/exposure_sentinel.py::SentinelCommandSet.do_lazysentinel","name":"do_lazysentinel","qualname":"SentinelCommandSet.do_lazysentinel","kind":"method","file":"cli/commands/exposure_sentinel.py","line":21,"end_line":51,"language":"py","signature":"def do_lazysentinel(self, line: str) -> None","params":[{"name":"line","annotation":"str","default":"","kind":"positional"}],"returns":"None","decorators":["cmd2.with_category(miscellaneous_category)"],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Run the internal sentinel lifecycle.","description":"Usage:\n    lazysentinel provision <cidr>... [--spool-in <path>]\n    lazysentinel dispatch <client_id> [--from-provision <id>] [--send]\n    lazysentinel ingest <spool path> [--feed <path>] [--json]\n    lazysentinel checks <target> [--feed <path>]\n\n``provision`` renders one read-only copy-paste blob that sweeps a\nprivate range from inside the network (beacon, or any box with\nnmap). ``dispatch`` wraps the blob in a c2_exec line. ``ingest``\nparses the spool back into sightings, generates exposure reports\nper host and considers autofire. ``checks`` renders read-only\nvalidation commands for the ingested services.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"cli/commands/exposure_sentinel.py::SentinelCommandSet","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":false,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":["core/console.py::print_error"],"called_by":[]}
